     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day. This order is about twice that. Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, and kidney and liver function being normal doesn't change that.\n\nSome possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** This could be 850 mg PO twice daily with meals, or a different split.\n- **Another dose or frequency.** Tell me what you meant.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
